# Commit messages (Hublio)

When generating or writing a git commit message for this repository, **always** follow Conventional Commits as defined in `docs/26-development-workflow.md`.

## Format

```text
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short summary in imperative mood>

[optional body — why, not what]

[optional footer]
```

### Rules

* Subject line ≤ ~72 characters.
* Imperative mood: “add”, “fix”, “wrap” — not “added” / “fixes”.
* Focus the subject on **why** / outcome; put file lists only in the body if needed.
* One logical change per commit.
* Do **not** mention Cursor, Copilot, or that the message was AI-generated.
* Do **not** wrap the subject in quotes or markdown code fences.
* English preferred (matches existing history and docs). Vietnamese only if the user explicitly asks.

### Types

| Type | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Internal change, same behavior |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, CI, repo hygiene |
| `perf` | Performance |
| `build` | Build system / Docker / Makefile |
| `ci` | CI workflow only |
| `style` | Formatting only (no logic) |

### Scopes (monorepo — use when clear)

| Scope | Area |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `apps/api` Go backend |
| `web` | `apps/web` Next.js workspace |
| `admin` | `apps/admin` |
| `ui` | `packages/ui` |
| `sdk` | `packages/sdk` |
| `deploy` | `deploy/` Docker/compose |
| `docs` | `docs/`, root README/AGENTS |
| `ci` | `.github/workflows` |

Omit scope when the change spans multiple areas or is purely repo-wide.

### Examples

```text
feat(api): wrap HTTP listen address conflicts as CONFLICT
```

```text
fix(web): point BFF clients at workspace-scoped API keys
```

```text
chore: migrate Go module and Next apps into monorepo layout
```

```text
docs: document hybrid BFF API access and local Quick start
```

```text
fix(api): surface fatal logs on stderr in production mode

Production previously wrote only to apps/api/logs/app.log, so
`make server` failures looked like a silent exit status 1.
```

## IDE “Generate Commit Message”

Cursor / VS Code Source Control generate-commit must produce a message that matches this format exactly — single subject line first; body only when the diff needs rationale.
